_tests/node_modules/
_tests/evidence/html-report/
_tests/test-results/

# ── Secrets & credentials (Helix Constitution §11.4.10 — no secrets in VCS) ──
# MCP server configs frequently embed API keys / tokens.
.mcp.json
# Environment / key-material files, at any depth.
.env
*.env
.env.*
api_keys.sh
**/api_keys.sh
secrets.sh
**/secrets.sh
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# ── OpenDesign daemon logs & generated tool output (§11.4.77) ───────────────
_tools/od/*.log
_tools/od/**/*.log
_tools/od/out/
od-daemon*.log
opendesign*.log

# ── Scratchpad / transient working files ───────────────────────────────────
scratchpad/
.scratchpad/
*.tmp
*.bak

# ── Editor / OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Generated binary evidence that must not be tracked ─────────────────────
# Root-level generated PNG/PDF proofs (scoped to root so nested, already-tracked
# evidence trees are untouched). The negation below is a belt-and-suspenders
# guard so the intentionally-tracked _tests/evidence/ tree is never ignored.
/*.png
/*.pdf
!_tests/evidence/

# Python bytecode (never track)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ephemeral playwright/temp installs (never track)
.ptmp/
**/.ptmp/

# Wizard test-run evidence (generated by scripts/test-setup-agents-wizard.sh)
.test-evidence/

# Superpowers scratch (progress ledger)
.superpowers/

# Resilient reindex log (generated)
.lumen-reindex.log

# Generated by the wizard each run
MANUAL-STEPS.md

# Timestamped safety backups (*.bak.<timestamp>) - keep locally, never commit.
# They contain the pre-fix content, including old hardcoded paths.
*.bak.*

# ashlr genome: keep the curated, repo-grounded files in version control so the
# routing context is shared, but ignore machine-generated churn. discoveries-auto.md
# is raw {"stdout":...} tool dumps that dilute retrieval against the curated
# discoveries.md, and proposals.jsonl is an append-only session log.
.ashlrcode/genome/knowledge/discoveries-auto.md
.ashlrcode/genome/proposals.jsonl

# Playwright browser cache (CI caches this path via actions/cache; locally it
# materialises when PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH points here). Never commit it.
.pw-browsers/

# Local .git backup snapshots of submodules (multi-GB pack files). Never commit.
workshop-git-backup-*/

# ── Docs Chain (§11.4.106) runtime state and per-run evidence ──────────────
# The per-context YAML under .docs_chain/contexts/ IS tracked — it is the
# binding itself, and an untracked binding binds nothing (§11.4.215). Only the
# regenerable hash baseline and the per-run evidence pack are ignored, exactly
# as the docs_chain module's own .gitignore prescribes for a consuming project.
# Regeneration mechanism per §11.4.77: `docs_chain sync --all`.
.docs_chain/state.json
*.docs_chain.tmp
/qa-results/docs_chain/

# ── §11.4.65 Markdown exports: TRACKED, on the operator decision of 2026-09-09 ─
# REVERSED. The block that stood here ignored every `.html` + `.pdf` sibling
# Docs Chain derives from an in-scope `.md`. Its reasoning is KEPT below rather
# than deleted, because it was a real measurement and the trade it named is
# real — it was simply decided the other way.
#
# THE OLD DECISION AND ITS EVIDENCE (2026-09-03), preserved:
#   "They are not tracked, for a MEASURED reason. The content-boundary gate
#    reads a text-bearing PDF via pdftotext and HTML as text, so each export
#    re-presents its source's full text to the detector. Measured on this tree:
#        tracked-only          LEAK — 11973 match(es)
#        + the 146 exports     LEAK — 24759 match(es)      +12786, +107%
#    Tracking them would therefore more than DOUBLE a gate that is already red
#    by design and must stay readable, while disclosing nothing new — every
#    export is a rendering of a `.md` that is already public. §11.4.30 forbids
#    versioning a build derivative and §11.4.77 is satisfied: the regeneration
#    mechanism is `docs_chain sync --all`, wired and gated."
#
# WHY IT WAS REVERSED, 2026-09-09, on an explicit operator decision:
#   Ignoring the exports made §11.4.65 compliance a WORKING-TREE property only.
#   A fresh clone carries no exports at all, so scripts/verify-docs-chain.sh —
#   which checks protections 1 and 2 ON DISK — is RED on arrival for every
#   consumer who has not first run a sync. §11.4.65's own word is "available",
#   and available cannot mean "available only to whoever generated it locally".
#   The §11.4.30 objection was weighed, not waved away: §11.4.30 forbids
#   versioned BUILD artefacts of the applications and services; a rendering that
#   another anchor mandates must EXIST is the deliverable, not its by-product.
#   The content-boundary cost is ACCEPTED and EXPECTED — that gate's count will
#   rise, and a rise caused by tracking renderings of already-public Markdown is
#   inherent to the mandate, NOT a new disclosure. It is recorded, not hidden.
#
# WHAT IS STILL IGNORED, and why — this is a NARROWING, not a blanket reversal:
#   * `/*.png` (above) — root-level generated PNG proofs. UNTOUCHED.
#   * `/*.pdf` (above) and `/*.html` (below) still ignore ROOT files BY DEFAULT.
#     Only the seven `umbrella-root` carrier siblings are negated, BY NAME. A
#     root-level generated proof therefore stays ignored exactly as before; only
#     a document export becomes trackable.
#   * `/qa-results/docs_chain/` — the per-run evidence pack. UNTOUCHED.
#   * `.docs_chain/state.json` — the regenerable hash baseline. UNTOUCHED.
#   * `_tests/evidence/html-report/`, `_tools/od/out/` and the other generated
#     trees keep their own directory rules. UNTOUCHED.
#   * Paths inside `.gitmodules`-declared submodules were never in scope of
#     these rules and are not now.
#
# The four blanket globs `/docs/**/*.{html,pdf}` and `/specs/**/*.{html,pdf}`
# are REMOVED — they were added by the 2026-09-03 block above and protected
# nothing else. Measured before removing them (2026-09-09): every `.html` and
# `.pdf` present under `docs/` and `specs/` is a `.md` sibling (4 of 4), and no
# script in this tree writes a non-sibling `.html`/`.pdf` into either tree.
# Residual risk, stated rather than hidden: a FUTURE generated report under
# `docs/` or `specs/` would now be trackable and would need its own rule here.
/*.html
!/README.html
!/README.pdf
!/CLAUDE.html
!/CLAUDE.pdf
!/AGENTS.html
!/AGENTS.pdf
!/QWEN.html
!/QWEN.pdf
!/GEMINI.html
!/GEMINI.pdf
!/CONTINUATION.html
!/CONTINUATION.pdf
!/Constitution.html
!/Constitution.pdf

# Pre-ingest hardlink backups (Constitution §9: a hardlinked backup before any
# destructive op). scripts/ingest.sh rewrites TRACKED corpus files —
# curriculum/passages.jsonl among them — through a NON-ATOMIC os.WriteFile, so
# an interrupted run can truncate the source of truth, and truncated JSONL
# parses fine. The backup is therefore mandatory, not optional.
#
# IGNORED BECAUSE THE COMMIT WRAPPER RUNS `git add .`. A backup is ~120 hardlinks
# to tracked content; committing one would duplicate the corpus into history
# under a timestamped path. Keep them beside the repo for recovery, never in it.
.workshop-ingest-backup-*/
# BROADENED, AND THE NARROW FORM WAS A NEAR-MISS. The rule above is a DIRECTORY
# pattern naming one workflow ("ingest"), so it matched neither a FILE backup nor
# any other workflow's. A pre-purge backup written here as
# `.workshop-kgterm-backup-<stamp>.jsonl` would therefore have been an untracked,
# NON-IGNORED copy of the private corpus sitting in the PUBLIC umbrella — and the
# commit wrapper runs `git add .`. Caught before it happened, by checking rather
# than trusting the claim that the narrow rule covered it.
#
# Both spellings, any workflow name, file or directory.
.workshop-*-backup-*
.workshop-*-backup-*/

# ── §11.4.93 / §11.4.95 workable-items SQLite SSoT ───────────────────────────
# The DATABASE ITSELF IS TRACKED and MUST NEVER be added here. §11.4.95 is
# explicit: "TRACKED in git at canonical path docs/workable_items.db. NEVER
# gitignored regardless of file-size or 'build-artefact-class' heuristics — the
# DB is NOT a build artefact, it IS authoritative source data." The paired
# mutation for scripts/verify-workable-items.sh adds it here and proves the gate
# turns red; if you are reading this because you were about to ignore the DB,
# that is the exact failure the gate exists to catch.
#
# What IS ignored is the transient WAL pair, which §11.4.95 names by hand:
# "SQLite's WAL mode produces transient *.db-wal + *.db-shm sidecars. Those ARE
# gitignored." Their state is checkpointed into the main .db file.
docs/workable_items.db-wal
docs/workable_items.db-shm

# Compiled Go binaries under _tools/ are build artefacts (§11.4.30). The source
# and the regeneration command are tracked; the binary is not.
_tools/workable-items/bin/
